Alsayf imports the pinned public template parser, catalog/loader, protocols,
input provider, and execution engine. Upstream runtime sources are not modified.
The local internal/nuclei adapter's engine initialization follows the wiring in
the upstream lib/sdk.go and lib/sdk_private.go, with an Alsayf command, output
writer, and progress/error collector. The upstream license is preserved here.

The SDK wrapper is not imported: v3.11.1 unconditionally invokes
installer.NucleiSDKVersionCheck during SDK initialization even after the SDK's
DisableUpdateCheck option. Alsayf initializes the public engine packages directly
and does not import the SDK, installer, or internal CLI runner.

Alsayf requires explicit local template/workflow paths, disables update checks,
does not configure cloud uploads or reporting integrations, and supplies a
disabled Interactsh client. Its catalog excludes template files containing
Interactsh URL markers. Headless, code, self-contained, DAST, global-matcher,
and file-template capabilities are not enabled. Template definitions are
validated before scanning. Native template execution and matchers are retained.

DNS uses supplied resolvers or addresses read from /etc/resolv.conf rather than
the engine's built-in public resolver list. Native output events are serialized
locally; extracted values are not masked. Configuration files follow Nuclei's
NUCLEI_CONFIG_DIR setting. An absent local ignore file is initialized empty
without downloading an upstream ignore list; an existing ignore file is kept.

No nuclei-templates distribution, browser, or other runtime executable is bundled
or automatically downloaded. Template contents determine assessment requests;
disabling background services does not restrict arbitrary template destinations.
